# Hostel Management System — Project Summary & Feature Guide

This Hostel Management System is a full-stack web application designed to automate, streamline, and digitize the daily operations of a student hostel. It provides dual-role portals (Warden/Admin and Student) to manage accommodations, track attendance with location-based verification, process fee billing, manage outpasses, log visitors, and resolve complaints.

---

## ⚙️ Architecture & Technical Stack

The system is built as a split-architecture full-stack application:

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Frontend [Client Browser - Vanilla Web]
        UI[HTML5 / CSS3 / Vanilla JS]
        LS[(Local Storage Session)]
    end
    
    subgraph Backend [Express API Server]
        API[Node.js + Express.js]
        PIN[30s Rotating PIN Generator]
        GEO[Geofencing & Time-Window Evaluators]
    end
    
    subgraph Database [Relational Storage]
        DB[(MySQL Database)]
    end

    UI -->|REST API Requests| API
    API -->|Queries / Transactions| DB
    UI <-->|Local Auth State Checks| LS
```

1. **Frontend**: Pure HTML5, modern CSS3 styling (harmonic color palettes, glassmorphism UI elements, micro-animations, fully responsive), and Vanilla JavaScript for asynchronous API calls (`fetch`), DOM rendering, and client-side routing guards.
2. **Backend**: Node.js with Express.js creating a RESTful API server.
3. **Database**: MySQL relational database holding normalized tables with structured foreign key constraints.
4. **Security**: Multi-tier authentication including client-side navigation guards and secure server-side password hashing using **bcryptjs**.

