## 🗄️ Database Schema & Data Model

The database (`hostel_db`) consists of **8 interconnected tables** mapped out below:

* **`rooms`**: Stores room configurations (`room_no`, `capacity`, `type` [AC/Non-AC], `status` [Available/Full]).
* **`students`**: Student profiles containing core data (`id`, `name`, `email`, `ph_no`, `dept`) and allocated room reference (`room_no`).
* **`users`**: Login credentials (`username`, `password` [hashed], `role` [admin/student], and a 1-to-1 `student_id` linking to the student profile).
* **`attendance`**: Daily log (`student_id`, `date`, `status` [Present/Absent], `method` [Manual/Smart Phone], `geofenced` status).
* **`complaints`**: Student-filed issues (`student_id`, `description`, `date`, `status` [Pending/Resolved]).
* **`fees`**: Billing records (`student_id`, `amount`, `due_date`, `status` [Unpaid/Paid]).
* **`leaves`**: Student outpass logs (`student_id`, `reason`, `from_date`, `to_date`, `status` [Pending/Approved/Rejected]).
* **`visitors`**: Visitor records (`name`, `relation`, `student_id` being visited, `entry_time`, `exit_time`).

